meta {
  name: 86 Radiology E2E Flow
  seq: 86
}

script:pre-request {
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // Radiology Flow E2E — folder-level setup (runs before every request here).
  //
  // Proves the FULL "New Radiology Flow" end-to-end, zero manual input:
  //   bootstrap (siteadmin -> tenant + business admin -> branch -> operator) ->
  //   SiteAdmin radiology catalogue template ->
  //   branch catalogue (radiology test in master data -> import into the branch) ->
  //   reporting doctor + outsource center ->
  //   patient -> radiology order (spawns a RadiologyStudy, SKIPS accession) ->
  //   process the study acquire -> report -> approve -> publish -> history -> print.
  //
  // Every id/token is captured by each request's post-response via bru.setVar(...)
  // - nothing is copied by hand. Just Run Folder, or click Next through 01 -> 38.
  // A per-run unique id (radRunId) keeps unique fields from colliding on re-runs.
  //
  // Token map (mirrors the proven EMI/TAT flows):
  //   siteAdminToken     - platform SiteAdmin (template + tenant create).
  //   businessAdminToken - tenant-level business_admin; BYPASSES per-permission
  //                        RBAC, so it does the RBAC-gated creates (master-data
  //                        radiology test, reporting doctor, outsource center).
  //   operatorToken      - branch-scoped receptionist; carries active_branch_id,
  //                        so it does the branch-level work (import, patient,
  //                        order, study processing - none of which are RBAC-gated).
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  if (!bru.getVar("baseUrl")) bru.setVar("baseUrl", "http://localhost:3000/api/v1");

  // Entry point - the SEEDED platform SiteAdmin (prisma/seed.ts). The ONLY
  // credential this flow assumes exists; tenant + users are created at runtime.
  if (!bru.getVar("siteAdminEmail"))    bru.setVar("siteAdminEmail", "admin@kalnostics.com");
  if (!bru.getVar("siteAdminPassword")) bru.setVar("siteAdminPassword", "SuperSecret1");

  // Known passwords this flow sets, so every login is automated.
  if (!bru.getVar("operatorPassword"))       bru.setVar("operatorPassword", "Str0ng@Pass1");
  if (!bru.getVar("bootstrapAdminPassword")) bru.setVar("bootstrapAdminPassword", "Str0ng@Pass1");

  // One-time per-run unique suffix + derived unique 10-digit national mobiles.
  // Guarded so it is computed once and reused across the whole run.
  if (!bru.getVar("radRunId")) {
    const n = String(Date.now());
    bru.setVar("radRunId", n.slice(-6));
    bru.setVar("adminBootstrapPhone", "95" + n.slice(-8)); // admin login identifier (^\d{10}$)
    bru.setVar("operatorMobile",      "98" + n.slice(-8));
    bru.setVar("operator2Mobile",     "93" + n.slice(-8));
    bru.setVar("patientMobile",       "96" + n.slice(-8));
    bru.setVar("doctorPhone",         "97" + n.slice(-8));
  }
}

docs {
  # Radiology Flow E2E — fully automated, click-Next end-to-end

  Reproduces the complete **New Radiology Flow** on our stack, from scratch, with
  no manual copy/paste: bootstrap a tenant + branch + a branch-scoped operator,
  build the radiology catalogue (SiteAdmin template + a branch-orderable radiology
  test), add a reporting doctor and an outsource center, register a patient, place
  a **radiology order**, then drive the generated `RadiologyStudy` through its
  whole lifecycle (acquire -> report -> approve -> publish) and print it.

  ## How to run
  Select this folder and **Run Folder**, or click **Next** through 01 -> 38. Each
  request captures the ids/tokens the next one needs via `bru.setVar(...)`. A
  `radRunId` is generated once per run so re-runs never collide on unique fields.
  The only credential assumed to exist is the **seeded SiteAdmin**
  (`admin@kalnostics.com` / `SuperSecret1`) - everything else is created at runtime.

  ## Flow (requests run in `seq` order)
  **Bootstrap:** 01 SiteAdmin login -> 02 create tenant + business admin -> 03
  business-admin login -> 04 branch (DIAGNOSTIC, modules enabled inline) -> 05
  operator user (`receptionist`, branch-scoped) -> 06 operator login
  (branch-scoped token).

  **Radiology catalogue:** 07 SiteAdmin radiology template (the global catalogue)
  -> 08 resolve the branch master data -> 09 create a radiology test in the master
  data (Business Admin, bypasses `master_data__add_test` RBAC) -> 10 import it into
  the branch (operator) -> 11 resolve the `branchRadiologyTestId`.

  **Config twins:** 12 radiology reporting doctor (Business Admin, `doctor__add`
  RBAC) -> 13 radiology outsource center (Business Admin, `outsource__add` RBAC).

  **Order -> study:** 14 patient -> 15 radiology order (`status: ORDER`, a single
  branch radiology test as its item). Because the order has a radiology item and
  is confirmed, the backend spawns exactly one **`RadiologyStudy`** (status `NEW`)
  in the same transaction - and, unlike a diagnostic order, it SKIPS accession
  (no `OrderSample`).

  **Process the study:** 16 list studies for the order (capture the `NEW` study)
  -> 17 acquire -> 18 report (fills findings/impression) -> 19 approve -> 20
  publish -> 21 status history (the full audit trail) -> 22 print the report PDF.

  **Order-edit regression (23-27):** a second radiology test -> import -> resolve
  -> **edit the order to swap in that item** -> verify the update path persists the
  new radiology ref AND generates its study (and tombstones the removed item's
  study). Guards the `OrderService.update()` bugs where radiology items were
  silently dropped and never entered the worklist on edit.

  ## Notes
  - Radiology study routes (`/radiology/studies/*`) are authenticated but NOT
    per-permission RBAC-gated, so the branch-scoped operator drives the whole
    lifecycle without extra grants.
  - The radiology pipeline runs PARALLEL to accession but skips specimen handling:
    a radiology order emits a `RadiologyStudy` worklist row directly, never an
    `OrderSample`.
  - `acquire` is legal straight from `NEW` (schedule is optional), so the flow goes
    NEW -> ACQUIRED -> REPORTED -> APPROVED -> PUBLISHED (validation is skippable).
}
